.TH BLUGON-LITE 1 "February 2026" "blugon-lite 1.0.0-lite" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
blugon-lite \- Blue Light Filter for X Window System (minimalist version)

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blugon-lite
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-once\fR]
[\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-interval\fR \fISECS\fR]
[\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-configdir\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-b\fR|\fB\-\-backend\fR \fIBACKEND\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
blugon-lite is a lightweight blue light filter for X Window System. It adjusts screen color temperature based on time of day, reducing blue light during evening hours to improve sleep quality.

This is a minimalist fork of blugon, optimized for lower RAM consumption (< 8MB) and reduced code complexity (202 lines).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.

.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-once
Apply gamma values for current time once and exit.

.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval [\fISECS\fR]
Set time between refreshes in seconds (default: 120).

.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-configdir ", " \-\-config [\fIPATH\fR]
Specify configuration directory (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/blugon or ~/.config/blugon).

.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-backend [\fIBACKEND\fR]
Choose backend for communication with X. Available: scg, xgamma (default: scg).

.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration files are read from ~/.config/blugon/

.TP
.B gamma
Gamma/temperature schedule file. Format: "hour minute value" where value can be temperature (Kelvin) or RGB gamma values (0.0-1.0).

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run as daemon:
.B blugon-lite

.TP
Apply once and exit:
.B blugon-lite --once

.TP
Use xgamma backend:
.B blugon-lite --backend xgamma

.TP
Custom refresh interval (60 seconds):
.B blugon-lite --interval 60

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/blugon/gamma
Gamma configuration file.

.TP
.I /usr/share/blugon-lite/configs/evening/gamma
Example evening schedule configuration.

.SH BACKENDS
.TP
.B scg
Uses Xrandr extension for gamma control. Requires libxrandr. Best quality.

.TP
.B xgamma
Uses xorg-xgamma command. More compatible but requires external dependency.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.

.TP
.B 12
Cannot open display (scg backend only).

.TP
.B 1
General error.

.SH SEE ALSO
redshift(1), sct(1), xgamma(1)

